**Summary of the two fixes:**

| Bug | Root cause | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| Duplicate processing | `dequeue()` had an `await` between checking `status == "pending"` and setting `status = "processing"`. The yield let other coroutines see the same job as still pending and grab it. | Moved `job["status"] = "processing"` before the `await asyncio.sleep(0.01)` so the claim is atomic (no yield point in the critical section). |
| Vanishing failures | `worker.py`'s `except` block caught the exception, printed it, but never called `queue.fail()`. Jobs stayed stuck in `"processing"` forever — never retried, never marked `"failed"`. | Added `queue.fail(job["id"], str(e))` in the except handler so failing jobs transition through the retry/fail state machine. |

No public method signatures were changed.
